    "text": "<math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Ph</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msup> <mtext>C</mtext> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </msup> <mtext>&#8196;</mtext><mtext>&#8203;</mtext><mtext>&#62;</mtext><mtext>&#8196;</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced><msup> <mtext>C</mtext> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math><br />In <math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Ph</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msup> <mtext>C</mtext> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </msup> <msup> <mtext>e</mtext> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> undergoes in delocalization while <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced><msup> <mtext>C</mtext> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> is stable due to the <math> <mrow> <mtext>+I</mtext></mrow> </math> and hyperconjugation effect of <math> <mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo><msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> group, because resonance is a predominant factor so the order is above one.<br />&nbsp;",
